# 📝 Finding Template

## Standard Format

```markdown
## [SEVERITY-##] Title

### Summary
One-sentence description of the vulnerability.

### Vulnerability Detail
Detailed technical explanation of the issue. Include:
- What is wrong
- Why it's wrong
- Relevant code flow

### Impact
Describe what can go wrong:
- Type of loss (funds, functionality, griefing)
- Who is affected
- Conditions required
- Estimated financial impact

### Code Snippet
https://github.com/protocol/repo/blob/commit/src/Contract.sol#L123-L145

```solidity
// Vulnerable code
function withdraw() external {
    uint256 balance = balances[msg.sender];
    payable(msg.sender).call{value: balance}("");  // Bug here
    balances[msg.sender] = 0;
}
\```

### Tool Used
Manual Review

### Recommendation
How to fix the issue:

```solidity
// Fixed code
function withdraw() external {
    uint256 balance = balances[msg.sender];
    balances[msg.sender] = 0;  // State update first
    payable(msg.sender).call{value: balance}("");
}
\```

### References
- [Similar exploit](link)
- [Documentation](link)
```

---

## Severity Guidelines

### Critical
- Unconditional direct loss of funds
- Protocol takeover
- Permanent DoS of critical functionality

### High
- Conditional loss of funds
- Significant economic damage
- Privilege escalation

### Medium
- Limited fund loss
- Griefing with cost to attacker
- Broken core functionality

### Low
- Minor issues
- Edge cases
- Unlikely scenarios

### Informational
- Gas optimizations
- Code quality
- Best practices

